{%- comment -%}
Paste this into the "Quadrant" tab of the lunch-lerum plugin's Edit
Markup screen (separate from the "Full" tab's template.liquid). Compact
version   for small Mashup panes - just today's lunch, no forecast table.

SIZING (adaptive - read this first; it supersedes every fixed size
mentioned in the older notes below): the pane is a fixed, non-scrolling
~400x240 box minus a 40px title bar, and anything taller than it is
cropped, so "as big as possible" means "as big as still fits TODAY'S
text", worked out per render in Liquid instead of one fixed size that has
to fit the worst case. Everything hangs off `pane_h` at the top of the
markup (170 = content height budget in px, deliberately a bit under the
~180px believed to be usable). If the real device shows unused room
under the content, raise it; if the bottom is cropped, lower it - it is
the only number to touch.

Layout: ONE table row, two cells (56% / 44%). The food icons now sit
at the top of the LEFT cell (nested table, same as before), so the
right cell (Dagens kock) gets the pane's full height instead of
sharing it with an icon row above it - that is what makes a much
bigger chef photo possible.

Left cell (dish): font is picked from 18/20/22/24/28/32/40px. For each
candidate a greedy word-wrap is simulated with character counts
(`d_cur*` / `d_lines*` - Liquid has no functions, hence one block per
size), and the LARGEST size whose wrapped height fits `text_room`
(pane_h - 20 label - 48 icon row when there is one) AND whose longest
word fits on one line wins. Long Swedish compounds are why the
longest-word check exists: at 32px "Fiskgratäng" would not fit the cell
width. Hyphens count as break points ("ost- och skinkpaj"), same as a
browser. Short text (a note like "Höstlov") gets 40px, a 60+ character
dish still gets 18-22px, all of them bigger than the old 16px
`description`.

Right cell (Dagens kock): name 20px semibold (1 line up to 12 chars,
else 2); description 20/18/16px - the largest size that still leaves
the photo at least `img_min` (80px), else 16px; the photo takes
whatever height is left (40-150px) through `max-height` (with
`max-width: 100%` and `width/height: auto` so its aspect ratio never
distorts). The 42 broforce portraits are 127-193px wide x 200px tall,
so the cell's ~159px width never limits the photo, its height does.

The chars-per-line numbers in the greedy-wrap blocks were calibrated
by rendering the real chef descriptions and ~55 realistic school
dishes in Chromium (DejaVu Sans as a slightly WIDER stand-in for
Inter, so real text should wrap the same or better) and taking the
largest value that never under-counted lines, minus one character of
margin. If a font size changes, redo that calibration rather than
nudging numbers by feel.

Checked locally at 400x240 (mini Liquid interpreter + Chromium): all
42 chefs x 18 dishes x 1/4 icons, weekend hemmamat, note-only days,
no-chef fallback - nothing exceeded `pane_h`. Chef photos come out
48-102px tall (median 84; was a fixed 55). The three chefs with the
longest name + description (Boondock Bros, Broniversal Soldier, Col.
James Broddock) only get 48px. NOT tested on the physical device -
TRMNL's own stylesheet wasn't available offline, so label height (20px)
and `.value` margins are assumptions. Check a few real days.

LAYOUT: the dish's food icon(s) sit in their own row at the very TOP of
the whole pane, centered, above both the "Dagens Lunch" text and the
"Dagens kock" column - previously a single small icon sat at the BOTTOM
of just the left (lunch) column. Icons are bigger now too (44px, up from
32px) since a dish can show several of them side by side (see
fetch.mjs's iconsForDish() - a dish like "Fiskgryta med lax och sej"
shows a pot + fish + salmon icon together, one per food/component
mentioned, instead of a single generic icon). 44px (not 60px) because
this pane has a fixed, non-scrolling height: an earlier 60px version
pushed the dish text + Dagens kock column entirely out of the visible
area (icons showed, everything below them vanished). The Dagens kock
photo/description also shrank (55px fixed height) to give the now-bigger
icon row room without pushing the rest off-pane. [SUPERSEDED - the photo
is now sized adaptively, see SIZING above.] The description was
originally truncated at 30 chars, which was too aggressive - see the
DESCRIPTION LENGTH note near the "Dagens kock" section below for why
that's now 50.

CAUTION - the dish-text/Dagens kock section below is a plain HTML
`<table>` (one `<tr>`, two `<td>` cells), NOT a `<div class="layout
                                                   layout--row">` with flex children. It used to be a flex row, and three
  separate attempts to fix it that way - a bigger flex-grow share on the
  text column, a smaller gap, and finally adding the `item` class every
  other working flex row in this repo already has - all failed
  identically on the real device: the two columns collapsed into one
  narrow vertical sliver, with the dish text wrapped one character per
  line and the Dagens kock photo squeezed into a thin strip. Every one of
  those looked completely fine in every check possible without the real
  device (tag balance, structure review), so don't trust that a `layout
  layout--row` + `item` combination here will actually render as two
  side-by-side columns just because it matches the working pattern
  elsewhere in this repo - something about this specific spot (maybe the
  preceding icon `<table>` sibling, maybe something else never isolated)
    breaks it in a way that wasn't tracked down. Switching to a plain
    `<table>` sidesteps the whole flex row mechanism, reusing the same
      "plain unstyled table, not TRMNL's styled component" trick already
      proven to work for the icon row above and for `template.liquid`'s
      forecast table. Column widths are set with `width="58%"`/`width="42%"`
      on the `<td>`s plus `table-layout: fixed` on the `<table>`, not with
        flex-grow. If you need to touch this again, test on the real device
        before trusting anything here, and prefer extending the table pattern
        over reintroducing a `layout--row` in this specific spot.

        FOLLOW-UP BUG (fixed): the table swap above fixed the sliver, but the
        first version of it still wrapped each `<td>`'s content in
          `<div class="layout layout--col layout--center gap--xsmall">` (a flex
            column) - and on the real device that made everything after the first
            child inside each cell disappear (only the "Dagens Lunch"/"Dagens
            kock:" labels showed; the dish description text and the chef photo
            were both just gone). Flexbox inside a table cell is a well-known
            cross-renderer trouble spot (cell height/flow doesn't compute the way
            it does in a normal block or flex container), so this file no longer
            puts a `layout--col`/`layout--row` flex container directly inside a
            `<td>` anywhere - plain `<div>`s with `text-align: center;` handle the
              centering instead, no flex needed since it's just stacked text/an
              image. The Dagens kock `<img>` also switched from `max-height: 34%`
              (a percentage height, which needs a sized ancestor to mean anything -
              a `<td>` with no explicit height doesn't give it one) to a fixed
                `max-height: 55px`. [SUPERSEDED by SIZING above - the photo height is now
                computed.]

                ICON CENTERING (superseded - see ICON TABLE AUTO-STRETCH further down
                for the current approach): the icon-row `<table>` used to rely on
                  `margin: 0 auto` alone to center itself, which looked fine with 3 icons
                  spread across most of the pane's width but was visibly stuck at the
                  left edge with only 1 icon (e.g. a day whose dish matched no keyword
                  and fell back to the generic bowl icon). `margin: 0 auto` centers a
                  block element only when its containing block gives it a definite width
                  to center within, which apparently wasn't happening reliably inside the
                  `layout--col` column here. Fixed AT THE TIME by wrapping the `<table>`
                    in a `<div style="text-align: center;">` and switching the table itself
                      to `display: inline-table;`, so it centered via `text-align` the same
                      way a run of inline content would, instead of depending on auto
                      margins. That whole approach was later replaced (once the icon table
                      moved inside the outer table's `<td>` - see ICON HORIZONTAL ALIGNMENT -
                        `display: inline-table` stopped sizing the table to its content in that
                        context) with an explicit Liquid-computed pixel width plus
                        `margin: 0 auto` again, which is what actually ships now.

                        WHOLE-PANE VERTICAL CENTERING (fixed, two passes): the outer wrapper here
                        used to be plain `<div class="layout layout--col gap--xsmall">` - no
                          `layout--center` - which left everything pinned near the top of the pane
                          with a big dead gap below before the title bar, instead of centered
                          top-to-bottom. First pass added `layout--center` plus `height: 100%;`
                          (matching every other Quadrant template in this repo - broforce, banksy,
                          weather-yr - which all have `layout--center` on their outermost wrapper).
                          That noticeably improved things but real-device testing showed content
                          still sitting too high with room left at the bottom - `layout--center` on
                          a `layout--col` most likely only maps to `align-items: center` (cross
                          axis = horizontal), not `justify-content` (main axis = vertical
                          distribution), so it wasn't actually centering the column vertically
                          within the pane's height, just horizontally within its own width (which
                          the icon-table/text-align centering already handled anyway). Second pass
                          added `justify-content: center;` explicitly inline, which is the actual
                          CSS property responsible for vertical centering in a column flex
                          container - kept `height: 100%;` too, since `justify-content: center`
                          only has room to work with if the container's height is bigger than its
                          content's natural height in the first place.

                          Each icon <img> lives in its own plain <table>/<td> cell (not TRMNL's
                            styled table component, and not a bare flex row) - same rule as
                            bus-grabo/weather-yr: a bare <div class="layout layout--row"> wrapper
                              around multiple <img> siblings lets the surrounding layout stretch them
                              into a squashed sliver instead of their real shape on a real device;
                              table cells don't have that problem.

                              ICON HORIZONTAL ALIGNMENT (fixed; the icon table has since moved INTO the
                              left cell of the single-row table - see SIZING above - so it is centered
                              over the dish text automatically): the icon row used to be its own
                              separate full-width `<div style="text-align: center;">`, centered over
                                the ENTIRE pane width - which put it visibly to the right of "Dagens
                                Lunch"/the dish text below it, since that text only occupies the left
                                58% column once a Dagens kock exists. Fixed by moving the icon table
                                into the SAME two-column `<table>` as the dish-text/Dagens-kock row, as
                                  its own `<tr>` above it, with a matching `width="58%"` (or `colspan="2"`
                                    when there's no Dagens kock) on its `<td>` - so it's centered within the
                                      same 58%-wide column as the dish text, not the full pane. A `<table>`
                                        nested inside another `<table>`'s `<td>` is standard HTML (not the
                                          flexbox-in-`<td>` pattern the FOLLOW-UP BUG note above warns against),
                                            so this doesn't carry that risk. The gap that used to come from the two
                                            blocks being separate flex siblings with `gap--xsmall` between them is
                                            now `padding: 0 4px 4px` (extra bottom padding) on the icon row's `<td>`
                                              instead.

                                              LIQUID SYNTAX BUG (fixed): the first version of the alignment fix above
                                              gated the new `<tr>` on `{% if (today.lunch and ...) or (today.vegetarian
                                                and ...) %}` - parenthesized grouping in an `{% if %}` condition, which
                                                Liquid does NOT support (there's no operator precedence/grouping syntax
                                                at all - conditions are evaluated strictly left to right). This made the
                                                entire icon row silently stop rendering (no error shown, no icons, dish
                                                text/Dagens kock still fine) rather than throwing something obviously
                                                wrong - a much sneakier failure than the earlier device-only layout
                                                bugs, since this one would likely fail in ANY Liquid renderer, not just
                                                TRMNL's. Fixed by computing a plain boolean with `{% assign %}` first
                                                (`show_icon_row`), then a single flat `{% if show_icon_row %}` - no
                                                parentheses, no mixed and/or precedence to get wrong.

                                                ICON SPACING (fixed, icons/ asset fix, not this file): the macintosh
                                                and cheese icons had 19-25% built-in blank margin per side inside their
                                                own 128x128 canvas (see generate-icons.mjs's macintoshIcon()/
                                                cheeseIcon()), vs. ~9.4% (3/32 grid cells) for almost every other icon
                                                in the set - so even with zero padding between their `<td>`s, this
                                                  specific pair looked much farther apart than e.g. the fish+salmon pair
                                                  does. Removed the icon `<td>`s' `padding: 0 2px` (now `padding: 0`) AND
                                                    regenerated both icons with their artwork widened to match the ~9.4%
                                                    convention - see generate-icons.mjs and the Python port in the repo
                                                    history for the exact rescale. Both fixes needed: padding alone only
                                                    closed ~4px of an ~18px gap that was mostly baked into the icons
                                                    themselves.

                                                    ICON TABLE AUTO-STRETCH (fixed): even after the padding + artwork fixes
                                                    above, the gap between 2+ icons was still huge - roughly 3x an icon's
                                                    own width, way more than a few px of internal margin could explain.
                                                    Root cause: the inner icon `<table>` relied on `display: inline-table`
                                                      to size itself to its content (so `margin: 0 auto` - or the wrapping
                                                      `text-align: center` div used even earlier - could center it as a
                                                      compact block). That table now lives nested inside the OUTER table's
                                                      `<td>` (see ICON HORIZONTAL ALIGNMENT above) instead of being a
                                                        top-level child of the pane, and something about that context - most
                                                        likely `display: inline-table` not being honored the way a real browser
                                                        honors it - let the inner table stretch to fill its container's full
                                                        width, with its 2 auto-sized `<td>`s each grabbing half of that (much
                                                          too generous) space and centering their own image within it
                                                          independently, pushing the icons far apart instead of tight together.
                                                          Fixed by computing an EXACT pixel width for the inner table with Liquid
                                                          math (`{{ icon_count | times: 44 }}px`, one `{% assign %}` per branch -
                                                          `times` is a standard Liquid filter, unlike the parenthesized
                                                          conditions the LIQUID SYNTAX BUG note above warns about) instead of
                                                          relying on `display: inline-table` to size it implicitly, giving each
                                                          inner `<td>` an explicit `width: 44px` too, and switching back to
                                                            `margin: 0 auto` for centering (which only works reliably with a
                                                            definite width - exactly what the explicit pixel width now provides).
                                                            No more `display: inline-table` or auto-sized cells anywhere in this
                                                            file.

                                                            Dish text (history - now `class="value"` at an adaptive 18-40px, truncated
                                                            at 64, see SIZING above): switched from `value value--small` (truncated to 40 chars,
                                                            which is what was cutting dish names off mid-word - "Fiskgryta med lax
                                                            och sej serveras me...") to the `description` class, truncated much more
                                                            generously at 70 chars (comfortably fits every dish in the autumn term
                                                            menu - the longest is ~63 chars - so in practice it never actually cuts
                                                            a real dish short) instead of 40. Not literally unlimited: with the
                                                            pane's fixed non-scrolling height, a truly unbounded dish name could
                                                            wrap into enough lines to push the rest of the content off-pane the same
                                                            way the 60px icons briefly did (see above) - 70 is a safety ceiling that
                                                            every real dish stays well under, not a visible truncation in practice.
                                                            `description` is deliberately smaller/lighter than `value` (matches the
                                                            size already used for "Dagens kock"'s own description line below) so a
                                                            long dish name still fits comfortably in this small pane.

                                                            Bug fix (pre-existing, kept): this used to check ONLY today.lunch, so on
                                                            a day where only "Dagens Gröna" (vegetarian) was published (today.lunch
                                                            is null), it fell through all the way to the "No lunch info" fallback
                                                            even though a valid dish existed. Shows whichever of the two is actually
                                                            available, preferring Lunch when both exist (Full view shows both side
                                                            by side; Quadrant only has room for one).

                                                            Weekend note: skolmat never has data on Lördag/Söndag, so on weekends
                                                            this pane shows the hemmamat (home food) dish for whichever of the two
                                                            today actually is, instead of the generic "HELGn" text - more useful in
                                                            this small a space than a message that's just explaining an absence.
                                                            Hemmamat dishes don't get food icons (no keyword matching is done for
                                                            them), so there's no icon row on weekends - the pane just starts with
                                                            the "Hemmamat <day>" label instead.

                                                              "Dagens kock" (right column): unrelated in content to the lunch data -
                                                              it's today's random pick from the broforce plugin's own portrait roster
                                                              (see fetch.mjs's pickDagensKock()), shown as a "Dagens kock:" label,
                                                              picture, name, and a short Swedish description underneath (fetch.mjs
                                                              translates broforce's English description via
                                                              DAGENS_KOCK_DESCRIPTIONS_SV - broforce's own Quadrant/Full stay English,
                                                              this translation is lunch-lerum-only).

                                                              DESCRIPTION LENGTH (fixed): the description was truncated at 30 chars,
                                                              which cut most of the roster's Swedish descriptions off mid-word/mid-name
                                                              (e.g. "Lee från Enter the Dragon / Bru..." never got to show "Bruce
                                                              Lee" at all). The longest entry in DAGENS_KOCK_DESCRIPTIONS_SV is 47
                                                              chars ("Connor och Murphy MacManus från Boondock Saints"), so 30 was
                                                              cutting the majority of the ~42-entry roster short, not just an edge
                                                              case. Raised to 50 - comfortably above the real max, same "safety
                                                              ceiling every real value stays under" reasoning as the dish text's
                                                              truncate: 70 above.
                                                              {%- endcomment -%}

                                                              {% assign pane_h = 170 %}

                                                              {% assign show_icon_row = false %}
                                                              {% assign icon_row_width = 0 %}
                                                              {% if today.lunch and today.lunch_icon_urls.size > 0 %}
                                                              {% assign show_icon_row = true %}
                                                              {% assign icon_row_width = today.lunch_icon_urls.size | times: 44 %}
                                                              {% elsif today.vegetarian and today.vegetarian_icon_urls.size > 0 %}
                                                              {% assign show_icon_row = true %}
                                                              {% assign icon_row_width = today.vegetarian_icon_urls.size | times: 44 %}
                                                              {% endif %}

                                                              {%- comment -%} ===== What the left column says ===== {%- endcomment -%}
                                                              {% assign dish_label = "" %}
                                                              {% assign dish_text = "" %}
                                                              {% if today.lunch %}
                                                              {% assign dish_label = "Dagens Lunch" %}
                                                              {% assign dish_text = today.lunch | truncate: 64 %}
                                                              {% elsif today.vegetarian %}
                                                              {% assign dish_label = "Dagens Gröna" %}
                                                              {% assign dish_text = today.vegetarian | truncate: 64 %}
                                                              {% elsif today.is_weekend %}
                                                              {% assign dish_label = "Hemmamat " | append: today.weekday %}
                                                              {% if today.hemmamat and today.weekday == "Lördag" %}
                                                              {% assign hm_lunch = today.hemmamat.lordag.lunch | truncate: 28 %}
                                                              {% assign hm_middag = today.hemmamat.lordag.middag | truncate: 28 %}
                                                              {% assign dish_text = hm_lunch | append: " / " | append: hm_middag %}
                                                              {% elsif today.hemmamat %}
                                                              {% assign hm_lunch = today.hemmamat.sondag.lunch | truncate: 28 %}
                                                              {% assign hm_middag = today.hemmamat.sondag.middag | truncate: 28 %}
                                                              {% assign dish_text = hm_lunch | append: " / " | append: hm_middag %}
                                                              {% else %}
                                                              {% assign dish_text = today.note %}
                                                              {% endif %}
                                                              {% elsif today.note %}
                                                              {% assign dish_label = today.weekday %}
                                                              {% assign dish_text = today.note %}
                                                              {% else %}
                                                              {% assign dish_text = "No lunch info" %}
                                                              {% endif %}

                                                              {%- comment -%} ===== Biggest dish font that still fits (see SIZING note above) ===== {%- endcomment -%}
                                                              {% assign text_room = pane_h | minus: 20 %}
                                                              {% if show_icon_row %}
                                                              {% assign text_room = text_room | minus: 48 %}
                                                              {% endif %}
                                                              {% assign dish_words = dish_text | replace: "-", "- " | split: " " %}
                                                              {% assign longest_word = 0 %}
                                                              {% assign d_cur1 = 0 %}{% assign d_lines1 = 1 %}
                                                              {% assign d_cur2 = 0 %}{% assign d_lines2 = 1 %}
                                                              {% assign d_cur3 = 0 %}{% assign d_lines3 = 1 %}
                                                              {% assign d_cur4 = 0 %}{% assign d_lines4 = 1 %}
                                                              {% assign d_cur5 = 0 %}{% assign d_lines5 = 1 %}
                                                              {% assign d_cur6 = 0 %}{% assign d_lines6 = 1 %}
                                                              {% for w in dish_words %}
                                                              {% assign wl = w | size %}
                                                              {% if wl > longest_word %}{% assign longest_word = wl %}{% endif %}
                                                              {% if d_cur1 == 0 %}{% assign d_cur1 = wl %}
                                                              {% else %}{% assign d_next = d_cur1 | plus: 1 | plus: wl %}
                                                              {% if d_next <= 17 %}{% assign d_cur1 = d_next %}
                                                                {% else %}{% assign d_lines1 = d_lines1 | plus: 1 %}{% assign d_cur1 = wl %}{% endif %}
                                                                {% endif %}
                                                                {% if d_cur2 == 0 %}{% assign d_cur2 = wl %}
                                                                {% else %}{% assign d_next = d_cur2 | plus: 1 | plus: wl %}
                                                                {% if d_next <= 15 %}{% assign d_cur2 = d_next %}
                                                                  {% else %}{% assign d_lines2 = d_lines2 | plus: 1 %}{% assign d_cur2 = wl %}{% endif %}
                                                                  {% endif %}
                                                                  {% if d_cur3 == 0 %}{% assign d_cur3 = wl %}
                                                                  {% else %}{% assign d_next = d_cur3 | plus: 1 | plus: wl %}
                                                                  {% if d_next <= 14 %}{% assign d_cur3 = d_next %}
                                                                    {% else %}{% assign d_lines3 = d_lines3 | plus: 1 %}{% assign d_cur3 = wl %}{% endif %}
                                                                    {% endif %}
                                                                    {% if d_cur4 == 0 %}{% assign d_cur4 = wl %}
                                                                    {% else %}{% assign d_next = d_cur4 | plus: 1 | plus: wl %}
                                                                    {% if d_next <= 11 %}{% assign d_cur4 = d_next %}
                                                                      {% else %}{% assign d_lines4 = d_lines4 | plus: 1 %}{% assign d_cur4 = wl %}{% endif %}
                                                                      {% endif %}
                                                                      {% if d_cur5 == 0 %}{% assign d_cur5 = wl %}
                                                                      {% else %}{% assign d_next = d_cur5 | plus: 1 | plus: wl %}
                                                                      {% if d_next <= 8 %}{% assign d_cur5 = d_next %}
                                                                        {% else %}{% assign d_lines5 = d_lines5 | plus: 1 %}{% assign d_cur5 = wl %}{% endif %}
                                                                        {% endif %}
                                                                        {% if d_cur6 == 0 %}{% assign d_cur6 = wl %}
                                                                        {% else %}{% assign d_next = d_cur6 | plus: 1 | plus: wl %}
                                                                        {% if d_next <= 7 %}{% assign d_cur6 = d_next %}
                                                                          {% else %}{% assign d_lines6 = d_lines6 | plus: 1 %}{% assign d_cur6 = wl %}{% endif %}
                                                                          {% endif %}
                                                                          {% endfor %}
                                                                          {% assign dish_fs = 18 %}{% assign dish_lh = 20 %}
                                                                          {% assign d_h = d_lines1 | times: 23 %}
                                                                          {% if d_h <= text_room and longest_word <= 17 %}{% assign dish_fs = 20 %}{% assign dish_lh = 23 %}{% endif %}
                                                                            {% assign d_h = d_lines2 | times: 25 %}
                                                                            {% if d_h <= text_room and longest_word <= 15 %}{% assign dish_fs = 22 %}{% assign dish_lh = 25 %}{% endif %}
                                                                              {% assign d_h = d_lines3 | times: 27 %}
                                                                              {% if d_h <= text_room and longest_word <= 14 %}{% assign dish_fs = 24 %}{% assign dish_lh = 27 %}{% endif %}
                                                                                {% assign d_h = d_lines4 | times: 31 %}
                                                                                {% if d_h <= text_room and longest_word <= 11 %}{% assign dish_fs = 28 %}{% assign dish_lh = 31 %}{% endif %}
                                                                                  {% assign d_h = d_lines5 | times: 36 %}
                                                                                  {% if d_h <= text_room and longest_word <= 8 %}{% assign dish_fs = 32 %}{% assign dish_lh = 36 %}{% endif %}
                                                                                    {% assign d_h = d_lines6 | times: 44 %}
                                                                                    {% if d_h <= text_room and longest_word <= 7 %}{% assign dish_fs = 40 %}{% assign dish_lh = 44 %}{% endif %}

                                                                                      {%- comment -%} ===== Dagens kock: description font + how tall the photo can be ===== {%- endcomment -%}
                                                                                      {% if today.dagens_kock %}
                                                                                      {% assign kname_lines = 1 %}
                                                                                      {% if today.dagens_kock.name.size > 12 %}{% assign kname_lines = 2 %}{% endif %}
                                                                                      {% assign kname_h = kname_lines | times: 22 %}
                                                                                      {% assign kdesc = today.dagens_kock.description | truncate: 50 %}
                                                                                      {% assign kdesc_words = kdesc | replace: "-", "- " | split: " " %}
                                                                                      {% assign img_room = pane_h | minus: 24 | minus: kname_h %}
                                                                                      {% assign img_min = 80 %}
                                                                                      {% assign k_cur1 = 0 %}{% assign k_lines1 = 1 %}
                                                                                      {% assign k_cur2 = 0 %}{% assign k_lines2 = 1 %}
                                                                                      {% assign k_cur0 = 0 %}{% assign k_lines0 = 1 %}
                                                                                      {% for w in kdesc_words %}
                                                                                      {% assign wl = w | size %}
                                                                                      {% if k_cur0 == 0 %}{% assign k_cur0 = wl %}
                                                                                      {% else %}{% assign k_next = k_cur0 | plus: 1 | plus: wl %}
                                                                                      {% if k_next <= 18 %}{% assign k_cur0 = k_next %}
                                                                                        {% else %}{% assign k_lines0 = k_lines0 | plus: 1 %}{% assign k_cur0 = wl %}{% endif %}
                                                                                        {% endif %}
                                                                                        {% if k_cur1 == 0 %}{% assign k_cur1 = wl %}
                                                                                        {% else %}{% assign k_next = k_cur1 | plus: 1 | plus: wl %}
                                                                                        {% if k_next <= 15 %}{% assign k_cur1 = k_next %}
                                                                                          {% else %}{% assign k_lines1 = k_lines1 | plus: 1 %}{% assign k_cur1 = wl %}{% endif %}
                                                                                          {% endif %}
                                                                                          {% if k_cur2 == 0 %}{% assign k_cur2 = wl %}
                                                                                          {% else %}{% assign k_next = k_cur2 | plus: 1 | plus: wl %}
                                                                                          {% if k_next <= 11 %}{% assign k_cur2 = k_next %}
                                                                                            {% else %}{% assign k_lines2 = k_lines2 | plus: 1 %}{% assign k_cur2 = wl %}{% endif %}
                                                                                            {% endif %}
                                                                                            {% endfor %}
                                                                                            {% assign kdesc_fs = 16 %}{% assign kdesc_lh = 18 %}
                                                                                            {% assign kdesc_h = k_lines0 | times: 18 %}
                                                                                            {% assign k_h = k_lines1 | times: 20 %}
                                                                                            {% assign k_left = img_room | minus: k_h %}
                                                                                            {% if k_left >= img_min %}{% assign kdesc_fs = 18 %}{% assign kdesc_lh = 20 %}{% assign kdesc_h = k_h %}{% endif %}
                                                                                            {% assign k_h = k_lines2 | times: 22 %}
                                                                                            {% assign k_left = img_room | minus: k_h %}
                                                                                            {% if k_left >= img_min %}{% assign kdesc_fs = 20 %}{% assign kdesc_lh = 22 %}{% assign kdesc_h = k_h %}{% endif %}
                                                                                            {% assign kimg_h = img_room | minus: kdesc_h %}
                                                                                            {% if kimg_h < 40 %}{% assign kimg_h = 40 %}{% endif %}
                                                                                              {% if kimg_h > 150 %}{% assign kimg_h = 150 %}{% endif %}
                                                                                              {% endif %}

                                                                                              <div class="layout layout--col layout--center gap--xsmall" style="height: 100%; justify-content: center;">

                                                                                                <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; table-layout: fixed;">
                                                                                                  <tr>
                                                                                                    <td style="border: none; vertical-align: middle; padding: 0 4px; text-align: center;"{% if today.dagens_kock %} width="56%"{% else %} colspan="2"{% endif %}>
                                                                                                      {% if show_icon_row %}
                                                                                                      <table style="width: {{ icon_row_width }}px; margin: 0 auto 4px; border-collapse: collapse; table-layout: fixed;">
                                                                                                        <tr>
                                                                                                          {% if today.lunch and today.lunch_icon_urls.size > 0 %}
                                                                                                          {% for icon_url in today.lunch_icon_urls %}
                                                                                                          <td style="border: none; padding: 0; width: 44px;"><img class="image image--contain image-dither" src="{{ icon_url }}" width="44" height="44" style="width: 44px; height: 44px;"></td>
                                                                                                          {% endfor %}
                                                                                                          {% elsif today.vegetarian and today.vegetarian_icon_urls.size > 0 %}
                                                                                                          {% for icon_url in today.vegetarian_icon_urls %}
                                                                                                          <td style="border: none; padding: 0; width: 44px;"><img class="image image--contain image-dither" src="{{ icon_url }}" width="44" height="44" style="width: 44px; height: 44px;"></td>
                                                                                                          {% endfor %}
                                                                                                          {% endif %}
                                                                                                        </tr>
                                                                                                      </table>
                                                                                                      {% endif %}
                                                                                                      {% if dish_label != "" %}
                                                                                                      <div class="label" style="text-align: center;">{{ dish_label }}</div>
                                                                                                      {% endif %}
                                                                                                      <div class="value" style="text-align: center; font-size: {{ dish_fs }}px; line-height: {{ dish_lh }}px; font-weight: 500; overflow-wrap: anywhere;">{{ dish_text }}</div>
                                                                                                    </td>

                                                                                                    {% if today.dagens_kock %}
                                                                                                    <td style="border: none; vertical-align: middle; padding: 0 4px; text-align: center;" width="44%">
                                                                                                      <div class="label" style="text-align: center;">Dagens kock:</div>
                                                                                                      <img class="image image--contain image-dither" src="{{ today.dagens_kock.image_url }}" style="max-height: {{ kimg_h }}px; max-width: 100%; width: auto; height: auto; display: block; margin: 2px auto;">
                                                                                                      <div class="value" style="text-align: center; font-size: 20px; line-height: 22px; font-weight: 600;">{{ today.dagens_kock.name }}</div>
                                                                                                      <div class="value" style="text-align: center; font-size: {{ kdesc_fs }}px; line-height: {{ kdesc_lh }}px; font-weight: 500;">{{ kdesc }}</div>
                                                                                                    </td>
                                                                                                    {% endif %}
                                                                                                  </tr>
                                                                                                </table>

                                                                                              </div>

                                                                                              <div class="title_bar">
                                                                                                <span class="title">Matn</span>
                                                                                                <span class="instance">{{ updated_display }}</span>
                                                                                              </div>